# fixedbugs, defect 2321, 2026-11-07: a construction labelling a field the
# record does not have, of a record declaring `a` twice. It was told that
# it missed `a:, a:`; read against each name's first declaration, its own
# mistake is told, the label `b` where the field is `a`, true whichever
# way the declaration is repaired.
record R
    a: i64
    a: i64  #~ field_declared_twice

function main()
    r = R(a: 1)  #~ wrong_label
    print(r.a)
